    ch1_title: 'One Coin',
    ch1_0: "A sleepy little town. It smells of fresh buns, empty promises and other people's debts. Perfect for getting rich.",
    ch1_1: "A battered cart rolls onto the square. A capybara peeks out. The look says “I'm here on purpose”.",
    ch1_2: "Hi, town. I'm Capy. One coin, a pile of ambition and zero Plan B.",
    ch1_3: "The dream is simple: my own shop. And here it is, a booth on the corner that has seen better days. And worse.",
    ch1_4: "The roof leaks, the sign hangs crooked, but hey, an awning. I'll call it “Everything for a Penny”. I already have a penny. Almost.",
    ch1_5: "That's how great stories start. And great loans. Tap the shop and earn. The first customer is already shifting nervously at the door.",

    ch2_title: 'First Friends',
    ch2_0: "A few days of tapping and the till is ringing. So many customers that Capy can't sell and panic at the same time. Someone else is needed.",
    ch2_1: "Hi! Any vacancies? I'm Spike the hedgehog. The résumé is prickly but honest.",
    ch2_2: "Prickly? For an interview that's probably a minus.",
    ch2_3: "It's a filter against shady customers. Also I count money faster than you can say “discount”.",
    ch2_4: "The register is yours. No probation: no time and no budget for it.",
    ch2_5: "Thanks. I promise not a single penny gets lost. Unless it gets stuck in the spines.",
    ch2_6: "Tip: open the \"Team\" tab and hire Spike. He boosts your tap power.",

    ch3_title: 'Someone Is Stealing!',
    ch3_0: "With Spike at the till business took off and the whole town heard about the shop. Along with the customers came someone who had no plan to pay.",
    ch3_1: "Capy, a pack of cookies is gone! All I caught was a striped tail and a very confident back.",
    ch3_2: "A striped tail and a confident back. I have a suspect.",
    ch3_3: "Nothing personal, it's just freelance. I'm Shnyr, the slickest raccoon in the neighborhood.",
    ch3_4: "You swiped my cookies. Give them back. Now.",
    ch3_5: "They're already a little... taste-tested. Call it a review. Tag, you can't catch me!",
    ch3_6: "Gone. Fine, we'll see who wins next time.",
    ch3_7: "Shnyr is sly but supposedly not evil. He'll be back. Hide the valuables and save your nerves.",

    ch4_title: 'The Strange Watch',
    ch4_0: "Hiding valuables from the raccoon, Capy rummages through the storeroom and finds something odd.",
    ch4_1: "A pocket watch. Old but stylish. The gold has darkened, the glass is cracked. Vintage, basically.",
    ch4_2: "It ticks. But the hands go backwards. Definitely not in the manual.",
    ch4_3: "Must be broken. Grandpa said: a watch that runs backwards is either broken or full of surprises.",
    ch4_4: "Surprises? Doubtful. But it's pretty. I'll keep it, no warranty.",
    ch4_5: "The watch ticked softly in the pocket, as if winking. Looks like that wasn't the last time.",

    ch5_title: 'Supermarket',
    ch5_0: "The watch ticks more confidently and business keeps climbing. The shop has grown into a proper supermarket. The whole town talks about Capy and “Everything for a Penny”, and new people join the team. Well, and animals.",
    ch5_1: "I'm Bodie, builder beaver. Heard you're expanding. Need planks? I'll send the invoice separately. And another one for politeness.",
    ch5_2: "I'm Zoya, sales. What displays... I'd sell snow in winter. Twice. With a markup.",
    ch5_3: "Hoo. I'm Sonia, accountant. Someone has to count these mountains of coins before they vanish on their own.",
    ch5_4: "Tonya. Security. Slow, but principled. And no favors.",
    ch5_5: "Come in, friends. I don't even know how to thank you.",
    ch5_6: "Thank us? I'm already first in line for the bonus.",
    ch5_7: "The team is growing. Hire new staff in the “Team” tab. Meanwhile someone in the dark is eyeing your register.",

    ch6_title: 'Shnyr in Trouble',
    ch6_0: "Late evening. The team has gone home and Capy is zoning out over the takings. Rain outside, and something stirs by the back door.",
    ch6_1: "Is someone sniffling? Shnyr, is that you?",
    ch6_2: "I'm not crying. It's the rain. On my face. Only on my face.",
    ch6_3: "Shnyr, why do you steal? Don't you have a home?",
    ch6_4: "I have a box behind the bakery. Friends, none. At all. Not even in group chats.",
    ch6_5: "If someone just said “hi” to me... But everyone yells “Catch the raccoon!”",
    ch6_6: "Hi, Shnyr. Just because. Come in, we have tea and buns.",
    ch6_7: "Seriously? Then I'm done stealing. Well... almost. Kidding. Probably.",
    ch6_8: "Since then Shnyr is no longer a thief but a friend. Mostly. Big things awaited everyone.",

    ch7_title: 'The Shopping Mall',
    ch7_0: "Months passed. Shnyr became a customer favorite and the team a real family, with minor fights over coffee. The shop grew into a store, then a supermarket, and now...",
    ch7_1: "A real shopping mall stands on the street, with a glass roof, a cinema and the smell of fresh pastry. Competitors quietly cry in a corner.",
    ch7_2: "The Capy Mall. From one coin. Who would have thought.",
    ch7_3: "Everyone built it, and the bonus goes to me. Lovely day.",
    ch7_4: "It's more fun with you than stealing. Though stealing was fun too.",
    ch7_5: "Thank you all. Without you this place would sell nothing but air.",
    ch7_6: "Suddenly something ticked loudly in Capy's pocket.",
    ch7_7: "My watch... Did it just come alive?",

    ch8_title: 'Finale: The Watch Ticks',
    ch8_0: "It did: the golden watch crawls out of the pocket and hangs in the air. The hands spin backwards, like in a bad movie.",
    ch8_1: "Hello, Capy. I waited long. Very long. An eternity, minus the coffee breaks.",
    ch8_2: "You can talk?!",
    ch8_3: "I'm the Watch of Time. I can turn back minutes. Refunds are not included.",
    ch8_4: "The mall is wonderful. But what if you could play it all again, with experience?",
    ch8_5: "Start over? But I already...",
    ch8_6: "Not lose, but build wiser. Friends stay. Knowledge stays. Coins don't. That's the economy.",
    ch8_7: "Wiser... Sounds not bad. I'll think about it.",
    ch8_8: "When you decide, just wind me up. I'm here. Ticking.",
    ch8_9: "Time travel is unlocked. Check the “Watch” tab: a new era is waiting.",

